			<item>
				<title>Secretion</title>
				<link>http://localhost:1313/posts/secretion/</link>
				<pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 10:23:33 -0400</pubDate>
				<guid>http://localhost:1313/posts/secretion/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;I begin by sitting on the porch, cross legged. I place my hands together, but I cant find my heart. Rain clouds the natural sounds of the night and I am floudering.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;After some time, my vision begins to blur. The shape of trees turn to suggestion. One cricket close to my right chirps steadily outside the downpour. I begin to count with each chirp. Twenty-two is the number I reach before I lose myself. A woman screaming in the dark. I run after her - my bare feet sloshing in the rain. Then I surface to a boom. I call the &amp;ldquo;secretion&amp;rdquo; quietly. As thunder passes, the cricket returns.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
